  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> of water at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is converted into steam at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> by boiling at atmospheric pressure. The volume of water changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;as a liquid to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>671</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;as steam. The change in internal energy of the system during the process will be (Given latent heat of vaporisation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2257</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, Atmospheric pressure <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
    "image": null
  },
